endpoints.responseShape:
[
  {
    "id": "uuid",
    "clinicId": "uuid",
    "physicianId": "uuid",
    "dayOfWeek": 0,
    "startTime": "09:00",
    "endTime": "09:15",
    "slotDuration": 15,
    "isActive": true,
    "createdAt": "2026-09-03T11:22:33.456Z",
    "clinic": { "name": "Cairo Clinic" }
  }
]

// A bare TOP-LEVEL ARRAY — not wrapped in {slots:[...]} or {data:[...]}.
// Empty case is `[]` (never null, never {}). Two distinct paths return `[]`: no PhysicianProfile (early return), and a physician with no matching active slots.
// Key order: the 9 TimeSlot scalars in prisma schema declaration order, then the included relation `clinic` last.
// `clinic` is the include `{ select: { name: true } }` — EXACTLY one key, `name`. NO id, NO address, NO phone. `clinic` is never null (clinicId is a required non-nullable FK with onDelete: Cascade).
// `dayOfWeek` is an Int 0..6 (0 = Sunday) — a NUMBER, not a string, and not validated on write so values outside 0..6 can be present.
// `startTime` / `endTime` are STRINGS "HH:MM", not Date/TimeSpan.
// `slotDuration` is an Int (minutes), DB default 30.
// `isActive` is always `true` in this response (hard-coded filter), but the key IS present.
// `createdAt` is an ISO-8601 UTC string with 3-digit ms and trailing Z.

{
  "count": 32,
  "message": "32 slots created"
}

// Exactly two keys, in this order. `count` is prisma createMany().count (an Int). `message` is the template literal `${created.count} slots created` — so the number appears TWICE, always in agreement, and the word is always plural even for 1 ("1 slots created").
// The created TimeSlot rows are NOT returned. The client must refetch GET /slots.

{
  "count": 96,
  "message": "96 slots created"
}

// Exactly two keys in this order. `count` is 0 when nothing was generated (createMany is skipped entirely and createCount stays 0) — the response is still 200 with {"count":0,"message":"0 slots created"}.
// The created rows are NOT returned; neither is the updated clinic. The client (ClinicDetailPage.handleSaveSchedule) ignores the body and refetches the clinic.
// Always plural in the message, even for 1.

{
  "message": "Slot removed"
}

// A single key. The deleted/updated TimeSlot is NOT returned, its id is NOT echoed, and there is no `count`, `success` or `deleted` key. The word is "removed", not "deleted" — and the route verb is DELETE while the DB operation is an UPDATE.
